// A docs board that faults on purpose with WireOverflow. A Route and an HTTP Handler are joined by
// one wire. A wire holds at most 256 requests in flight at once, and 257 scripted requests reach
// the Route on the same tick, tick 40. The first 256 go onto the request cable. The 257th finds the
// cable full, so the Route faults with WireOverflow and shows as faulted. A Route has no Fault
// port, so the fault rests on the Route itself. The Handler answers the 256 requests that got on
// the cable, and their replies cross the reply cable back to the Route. The run makes no outbound
// call.
//
//   row 1:                    +-----------+
//   row 2:   ROUTE 0 Out ===> | In  HTTP  |    cable 4 carries the requests,
//            ROUTE 0     <=== | HANDLER 1 |    cable 5 carries the replies
//   row 3:                    +-----------+
//   rows 4-5:                   Fault -b3---> SINK 2
//
// The Handler's Fault port, on its bottom middle cell facing south, has a belt to a Debug Sink,
// the usual place for a Handler's faults. The Handler's code never fails, so that belt stays
// empty.
//
// The script lists the 257 requests one per line. Entries on one tick apply in file order, and
// each request carries its number in its body.
//
// Handles mint in command order: the Route 0, the Handler 1, the Sink 2, the belt 3, then the two
// cables 4 (request) and 5 (reply), which the one DrawWire mints. The 9 commands and the history
// seal end the boot on tick 10.
//
// machine_kind u8 legend: ROUTE=9, HTTP HANDLER=10, SINK=7. DrawWire and Dock ports are catalog
// indexes: Route In=0, Out=1; HTTP Handler In=0, Out=1, Fault=2; SINK In=0.
//
// Format 2 adds two fields a page reads and the core never does: `title`, the name a page shows,
// and `captions`, the ticks a viewer pauses on, each with the machine it highlights and one
// sentence about what the board does on that tick.
Board(
    format: 2,
    title: "Too many requests on one wire",
    seed: 97,
    commands: [
        Place(kind: 9, cell_x: 2, cell_y: 2),        // 0: ROUTE
        Place(kind: 10, cell_x: 6, cell_y: 1),       // 1: HTTP HANDLER, 3x3
        Place(kind: 7, cell_x: 10, cell_y: 5),       // 2: SINK, Debug by default
        DrawBelt(cells: [(7, 4), (7, 5), (8, 5), (9, 5)]),                // 3
        Dock(belt: 3, endpoint: Tail, node: 1, port: 2),
        Dock(belt: 3, endpoint: Head, node: 2, port: 0),
        Configure(node: 0, config: Endpoint(path: "/orders")),
        Configure(node: 1, config: Factory(source: r#"// reply to each request
export default function (input, ctx) {
  ctx.command({
    status: 200,
    headers: {},
    body: "order received",
  }, 0);
}"#)),
        // One command mints both cables: 4 the request, then 5 the reply.
        DrawWire(from_node: 0, from_port: 1, to_node: 1, to_port: 0),
    ],
    script: [
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/orders", body: r#"{"order":1}"#)),
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/orders", body: r#"{"order":2}"#)),
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/orders", body: r#"{"order":3}"#)),
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/orders", body: r#"{"order":4}"#)),
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/orders", body: r#"{"order":5}"#)),
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/orders", body: r#"{"order":6}"#)),
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/orders", body: r#"{"order":7}"#)),
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/orders", body: r#"{"order":8}"#)),
